==============================================================================
O25 — compression curve  (exact psi, truncated explicit formula, no fitting)
==============================================================================
  psi(x)   = SUM_{p^k <= x} log p                       EXACT, from a sieve
  psi_K(x) = x - log(2pi) - (1/2)log(1 - x^-2)
             - 2 sqrt(x) SUM_{k<=K} [(1/2)cos(gL) + g sin(gL)]/(1/4 + g^2)
  L = log x, g = gamma_k, zeros paired as rho, conj(rho), rho = 1/2 + i gamma

  K_needed(x, target) = the SMALLEST swept K with the error <= the target.
  COMPRESSIVE at x : K_needed is not null AND K_needed <= pi(x).
  EXPANSIVE   at x : K_needed is null OR K_needed > pi(x).

